      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do you cover Knowsley Industrial Park?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. We attend commercial plumbing emergencies on Knowsley Industrial Park, Knowsley Business Park and the wider commercial estates around Kirkby. Same fixed rates as residential. No commercial premium. £80 an hour weekdays. We work with facilities managers and site teams to resolve faults fast." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do you handle right-to-buy and ex-council properties in Kirkby?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. A large share of Kirkby housing is former council stock now in private ownership. The original 1950s and 1960s pipework, copper heating runs and lead supply pipes are still in service in many of these homes. We know the standard layouts. We carry common replacement parts for the failures we see most often in this housing." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can I get a free boiler replacement through ECO4 in Kirkby?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Possibly. The ECO4 scheme provides free or heavily subsidised boiler replacements for qualifying households. Typically households on means-tested benefits or with a low EPC rating qualify. We can assess your Kirkby property's eligibility at a free survey visit. Call 0151 558 0334 and ask about ECO4 when you book." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do you cover lead supply pipe replacements?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Many Kirkby properties still have original lead supply pipes between the boundary stopcock and the kitchen. United Utilities has replaced most external sections in recent years, but the internal run from the boundary to the property is the homeowner's responsibility. We replace lead supply pipes with copper or MDPE plastic. Improves water quality and pressure." } },
