      <p class="pf-sub">Four steps that protect your property. We're usually only minutes away.</p>
      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">1</span><div><strong>Find the stopcock and turn it off</strong><p>For any water leak, the stopcock is your first move. In most Kirkby semis it's under the kitchen sink. Turn it clockwise to stop all water. We'll be there before you've cleared the cupboard out.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">2</span><div><strong>If you smell gas, get out</strong><p>Don't touch switches. Open windows as you leave. Call <a href="https://cadentgas.com/emergencies" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--orange);font-weight:700;">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first. Then us on 0151 558 0334 once the property is safe.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">3</span><div><strong>No heating? Check the pressure gauge</strong><p>Look at the gauge on the boiler. It should sit between 1 and 1.5 bar. Below 0.5, you can repressurise using the filling loop underneath. That fixes about half of all "no heating" calls. If it doesn't, call us.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">4</span><div><strong>Photograph the damage</strong><p>Take photos and video before you start cleaning. Insurance claims need evidence. We write our own fault report with photos as well, ready for your insurer or landlord.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
