      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an emergency plumber cost in Kirkby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>£80 an hour weekdays 9am to 5pm. £120 an hour weekends 9am to 1pm. £150 an hour out of hours, nights and bank holidays. 1 hour minimum on every call-out. Parts at cost. Most jobs cost £80 to £350. Same fair rates whatever the postcode. Written quote before work starts. No separate call-out fee.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you reach Kirkby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Faster than anyone else. We're based at 29 Park Road, Kirkby L32 2AL. That's a Kirkby address, not a Liverpool one. Most Kirkby calls reach us in 10 to 15 minutes. Some are under 5. A real person answers the phone any time of day or night.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COMMERCIAL</span>&nbsp; Do you cover Knowsley Industrial Park?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We attend commercial plumbing emergencies on Knowsley Industrial Park, Knowsley Business Park and the wider commercial estates around Kirkby. Same fixed rates as residential. No commercial premium. £80 an hour weekdays. We work with facilities managers and site teams to resolve faults fast.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">EX-COUNCIL</span>&nbsp; Do you handle right-to-buy and ex-council properties in Kirkby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. A large share of Kirkby housing is former council stock now in private ownership. The original 1950s and 1960s pipework, copper heating runs and lead supply pipes are still in service in many of these homes. We know the standard layouts. We carry common replacement parts for the failures we see most often in this housing.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">ECO4</span>&nbsp; Can I get a free boiler replacement through ECO4 in Kirkby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Possibly. The ECO4 scheme provides free or heavily subsidised boiler replacements for qualifying households. Typically households on means-tested benefits or with a low EPC rating qualify. We can assess your Kirkby property's eligibility at a free survey visit. Call 0151 558 0334 and ask about ECO4 when you book.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">LEAD PIPES</span>&nbsp; Do you cover lead supply pipe replacements?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Many Kirkby properties still have original lead supply pipes between the boundary stopcock and the kitchen. United Utilities has replaced most external sections in recent years, but the internal run from the boundary to the property is the homeowner's responsibility. We replace lead supply pipes with copper or MDPE plastic. Improves water quality and pressure.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are your engineers Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. All gas work is carried out by our own Gas Safe registered engineers. Verify our registration at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. It's illegal to work on gas without it. We provide gas safety certificates for all gas work in Kirkby.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">GUARANTEE</span>&nbsp; Do you guarantee your work?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Every job carries a 12-month workmanship guarantee. If something we fixed fails because of our work, we come back. No charge.</p></div></details>
